  "note": "Trace form (research/trace-harness.md) for L08: the static twins, served by scripts/trace.sh against PostgreSQL. Every outbound call goes to the harness's stub on 127.0.0.1, which answers as each request's upstream says. probes ask the twin's own pool (src/db.js) how many connections are checked out: while the stub answers the outbound call (pool-during, STB-09), and after the response against before the request (pool-after, STB-08). A request that leaks a connection runs on a twin of its own (restart), so one leak cannot exhaust the pool for the next. expect: error marks a request whose error path is the point; the trace schema makes it fail. defects are what the planted twin must report and the clean twin must not; every other request is a decoy, in both twins.",
